// Items: everything a survivor can carry. Schema: zombye_sim::items::ItemDef (validated on load;
// unknown fields are refused). All names and numbers are our own, using real-world weights and
// sizes so a new item's numbers can be guessed without a table.
//
//   id          lowercase letters, digits and _ (saves and loot tables name items by it)
//   category    Food, Drink, Medical, Tool, Material, Clothing, Bag, Weapon, Light or Junk
//   weight_kg   counts in full wherever it is carried (hands, pockets, bags, worn)
//   volume_l    room it takes in pockets, bags and furniture (held and worn items take none)
//   stack       how many share one slot (default 1)
//   tags        for rules that recipes and actions check: needs_tin_opener, opens_tins, cuts,
//               rippable, fire, fuel, light_source, junk, bandage, clean, disinfects, ...
//   two_handed  held in both hands (default false)
//   weapon      Some("id") of a weapon in weapons.ron: the item swings like it. Every weapon there
//               (but bare hands) should have an item here; one without gets a plain 1 kg item.
//   food, drink Some((hunger: 0..1 restored, thirst: 0..1 restored (negative: makes you thirsty),
//               uses: goes, spoils_hours: Some(game hours) or None)). Effects come with #11.
//   medical     Some((uses: n)). What it treats comes with #9 and #10 (by tag).
//   bag         Some((capacity_l: room it adds, carried: Back | Shoulder | Hand, slow: 0..1
//               speed lost while carried))
//   clothing    Some((covers: [Head, Torso, Arms, Hands, Legs, Feet], protection: 0..1,
//               layer: Base | Mid | Outer)). Two worn items can't share a body part and layer.
//   light       Some((radius_m, hours)): a light source (comes with night lighting).
//   color       grey-box colour on the floor, linear-ish RGB 0..1
[
